  "findings": {
    "person": "Person detail provides names, aliases, biography, dates, gender, profile and external references. Aliases have no per-name language label; translations do not make every name localized.",
    "organization": "Company and network have separate resource namespaces and detail/alternative-name/image reads. The inspected public API offers company name search but no network name-search endpoint.",
    "companyNaming": "The production-info guide requests Roman-script primary company names and allows original non-Roman names as alternatives; this does not identify the language of each alias.",
    "productionCompanies": "The guide excludes distributors and funding-only credits from production_companies, but the response does not distinguish animation studio from other production responsibilities.",
    "networks": "The guide describes original networks and explicitly scopes changing original networks by season; this is not a complete VOD availability list.",
    "movieCast": "The movie cast guide restricts cast to the original version, excludes dubbed/extended versions and motion-capture performers, and marks voice work in character text.",
    "tvCast": "Regular cast is defined per season. Episode guest-star guidance includes actors present in the original episode version. The API has no structured per-credit voice-language field.",
    "castIdentity": "Person IDs identify people; character text and credit IDs do not establish independent Character identities."
  },
